# The runner's per-machine record of the last run's results (2026-09-10).
#
# NOT COMMITTED, and the reason is in run_gates.py's own comment beside
# RECORD_PATH: several lanes run the suite in one shared tree, so a committed
# record would be rewritten whole by every run — hard-won law 11's
# whole-file-write hazard on a file that changes on every run rather than on
# every edit, where a pathspec commit publishes whatever another lane's run
# left there and a re-derived blob reverts one recorded four minutes ago.
#
# It gates nothing. No gate reads it, no verdict depends on it, and deleting
# it costs exactly one run's comparison — which the next run then says out
# loud rather than reporting zero changes.
last-run.json
last-run.json.tmp
